  "live_records": {
    "q-11323": {
      "dom_id": "step-q11323",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14212914/assets/36aaf58af536428c74cdb8f4c02c2b4f07e414422e8aea378c75d7abcff58cff.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{YX}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{XV}=b,$ $\\overset{\\to }{VZ}=c,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{YW}=d.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{XW}$ in terms of $a,b,c,$ and $d.$",
      "worked_solution": "We want to find a \"path\" from $X$ to $W$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$  \n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{XW}=\\overset{\\to }{XY}+\\overset{\\to }{YW},\n$$\n\nas shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14212914/assets/4758b51fd3dc076059d60e944de0ad8375bb304240365959d4c6cae94f95a535.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{XY}=-a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{YW}=d.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14212914/assets/e942d61c1f51c36dc6cd04f88ff5e37f538920a34c1af5bc780c47691567b668.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{XW} & =\\overset{\\to }{XY}+\\overset{\\to }{YW} \\\\  & =-a+d \\\\  & =d-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
