    "q-12046": {
      "dom_id": "step-q12046",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14212914/assets/4b441f7b59f59240141380711d5d380ea58cafa01f8a288f1e5c8bc7685650cf.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{PS}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=b,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PT}=c.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{QT}$ in terms of $a,b,$ and $c.$",
      "worked_solution": "We want to find a \"path\" from $Q$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,$ and $c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QT}=\\overset{\\to }{QS}+\\overset{\\to }{SP}+\\overset{\\to }{PT}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14212914/assets/f728becaa8903fc0aa17ea9d15dd7199447dd70eff5b4a3d2be5982f1eeca8a5.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{QS}=-b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{SP}=-a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PT}=c.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14212914/assets/055bb2c63c42defaa9f624f20b8ad92dd80f3d34b0d689def859b34785318749.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{QT} & =\\overset{\\to }{QS}+\\overset{\\to }{SP}+\\overset{\\to }{PT} \\\\  & =-b+(-a)+c \\\\  & =c-a-b.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-12046-a",
