    "q-143004": {
      "dom_id": "step-q143004",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14212914/assets/b0009b057eef7d5d4e380883f26442b2c4e5777e90c77a7fd7791506c87cbcd4.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDE$ shown above, which of the following are equal to the vector $\\overset{\\to }{BE}?$\n\nI. $\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}$\n\nII. $\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{DE}$\n\nIII. $\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}$",
      "worked_solution": "- For the $1$st expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE} & =(\\overset{\\to }{CB}+\\overset{\\to }{BA})+\\overset{\\to }{AE} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CE} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{BE}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $2$nd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC}+\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =(\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CD})+\\overset{\\to }{DE} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD}+\\overset{\\to }{DE} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BE}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the $3$rd expression, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE} & =\\overset{\\to }{BE}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
